<item><title>Former Kenya returnee&apos;s coffee firm buys up to a third of Bukinanyana harvest</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/former-kenya-returnee-s-coffee-firm-buys-up-to-a-third-of-aca5e3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/former-kenya-returnee-s-coffee-firm-buys-up-to-a-third-of-aca5e3/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Raphaël Yaminyibuka says his company spends 700 to 850 million Burundian francs per campaign to buy coffee, taking in half or as much as a third of the commune&apos;s crop.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:31:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
